        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(cron): emit session.maintenance.pruned diagnostic event on reaper pruning",
        "body": "#### What Problem This Solves\n\nClose #105198\n\nThe session reaper (`sweepCronRunSessions`) only emits a text log when it prunes cron run sessions. There is no structured diagnostic event, making it impossible to build dashboards or alerts around session-store maintenance health.\n\n#### Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a low-cardinality `session.maintenance.pruned` trusted diagnostic event, matching the existing `session.recovery.*` / `session.state` event patterns. Event carries only `pruned` (rows removed) and `swept` (boolean) — no session keys, store paths, or unbounded identifiers.\n\n#### User Impact\n\nNo visible impact. Operators gain structured metrics for session reaper throughput.\n\n#### Evidence\n\n- **Type check:** `tsgo` core passes; OTEL/Prometheus pre-existing `Cannot find module` errors unrelated\n- **Lint:** `oxlint` clean across all 5 files\n- **Tests:**\n  - `session-reaper.test.ts` — 22 tests (+2: emits trusted event when pruned > 0; no event when pruned = 0)\n  - `diagnostics-otel/service.test.ts` — 107 tests\n  - `diagnostics-prometheus/service.test.ts` — 17 tests\n  - No regressions\n\n- **Change scope:** 5 files, +103 lines. No new deps, no config/CLI/SDK/docs surface.\n\n- **Live proof** — real `sweepCronRunSessions` + `onInternalDiagnosticEvent` (vitest isolation, no mock):\n\n```\n[session.maintenance.pruned] pruned=2\n→ event: { type: \"session.maintenance.pruned\", pruned: 2, trusted: true }\n\n[session.maintenance.pruned] pruned=0 ← no event emitted\n\n[session.maintenance.pruned] retention disabled → swept=false, no event\n```\n\nThree scenarios verified: pruned sessions emit event, zero-prune is silent, disabled pruning is silent.\n\n- **Event shape:**\n```typescript\ntype DiagnosticSessionMaintenancePrunedEvent = DiagnosticBaseEvent & {\n  type: \"session.maintenance.pruned\";\n  pruned: number;\n  swept: boolean;\n};\n```\n\n- **OTEL:** `openclaw.session.maintenance.pruned` counter\n- **Prometheus:** `openclaw_session_maintenance_pruned_total` counter\n",
